## 5. Data

```yaml id=DATA kind=data
entities:
  - id: ENT-User
    name: User
    plain_name: Customers
    fields:
      - {name: name}
      - {name: phone}
      - {name: email, required: false}
      - {name: avatar, type: image, required: false}
      - {name: created_at, type: datetime}
    seed_guidance: Two sample customers, one restaurant owner and one courier with names that match the
      app locale.
  - id: ENT-Address
    name: Address
    plain_name: Delivery addresses
    fields:
      - {name: user, type: ref, ref: ENT-User}
      - {name: label, description: 'Home, Work, ...'}
      - {name: recipient_name}
      - {name: phone}
      - {name: line1}
      - {name: line2, required: false}
      - {name: landmark, required: false}
      - {name: city}
      - {name: postal_code}
      - {name: latitude, type: number, required: false, description: From the map pin}
      - {name: longitude, type: number, required: false, description: From the map pin}
      - {name: delivery_instructions, required: false}
      - {name: is_default, type: bool}
  - id: ENT-Cuisine
    name: Cuisine
    plain_name: Cuisines
    fields:
      - {name: name}
      - {name: image, type: image, required: false}
    seed_guidance: Eight cuisines such as pizza, burgers, noodles, salads, desserts, regional dishes,
      breakfast and healthy.
  - id: ENT-Restaurant
    name: Restaurant
    plain_name: Restaurants
    fields:
      - {name: name}
      - {name: description, type: text}
      - {name: image, type: image}
      - {name: cover_image, type: image, required: false}
      - {name: cuisine, type: ref, ref: ENT-Cuisine}
      - {name: rating, type: number, required: false}
      - {name: rating_count, type: int, required: false}
      - {name: delivery_fee, type: money}
      - {name: min_order, type: money}
      - {name: eta_minutes, type: int}
      - {name: is_open, type: bool}
      - {name: address, type: text}
      - {name: latitude, type: number}
      - {name: longitude, type: number}
      - {name: opening_hours, type: json, required: false}
    seed_guidance: 12 to 20 restaurants spread over a fictional city centre with coordinates, two of them
      closed right now.
  - id: ENT-MenuCategory
    name: Menu category
    plain_name: Menu sections
    fields:
      - {name: restaurant, type: ref, ref: ENT-Restaurant}
      - {name: name}
      - {name: position, type: int}
  - id: ENT-MenuItem
    name: Menu item
    plain_name: Dishes
    fields:
      - name: restaurant
        type: ref
        ref: ENT-Restaurant
      - name: category
        type: ref
        ref: ENT-MenuCategory
      - name: name
      - name: description
        type: text
      - name: price
        type: money
      - name: image
        type: image
        required: false
      - name: dietary_tags
        type: json
        required: false
        description: List such as veg, vegan, gluten_free, halal, spicy
      - name: is_available
        type: bool
      - name: is_popular
        type: bool
    seed_guidance: 8 to 25 dishes per restaurant in three or four menu sections, with a few marked popular
      and one sold out.
  - id: ENT-OptionGroup
    name: Option group
    plain_name: Dish option groups
    fields:
      - {name: item, type: ref, ref: ENT-MenuItem}
      - {name: name, description: 'Size, Toppings, Spice level'}
      - {name: kind, type: enum, enum: OptionKind}
      - {name: required, type: bool}
      - {name: max_choices, type: int, required: false}
  - id: ENT-OptionChoice
    name: Option choice
    plain_name: Dish option choices
    fields:
      - {name: group, type: ref, ref: ENT-OptionGroup}
      - {name: name}
      - {name: extra_price, type: money}
      - {name: is_default, type: bool}
  - id: ENT-Cart
    name: Cart
    plain_name: Cart
    fields:
      - {name: user, type: ref, ref: ENT-User}
      - {name: restaurant, type: ref, ref: ENT-Restaurant}
      - {name: delivery_address, type: ref, required: false, ref: ENT-Address}
      - {name: item_count, type: int}
      - {name: subtotal, type: money}
      - {name: delivery_fee, type: money}
      - {name: discount, type: money, required: false}
      - {name: total, type: money}
  - id: ENT-CartItem
    name: Cart item
    plain_name: Cart items
    fields:
      - name: cart
        type: ref
        ref: ENT-Cart
      - name: item
        type: ref
        ref: ENT-MenuItem
      - name: quantity
        type: int
      - name: selected_options
        type: json
        required: false
        description: Chosen option names with their extra prices
      - name: special_note
        required: false
      - name: unit_price
        type: money
        description: Dish price plus options
  - id: ENT-Order
    name: Order
    plain_name: Orders
    fields:
      - {name: user, type: ref, ref: ENT-User}
      - {name: restaurant, type: ref, ref: ENT-Restaurant}
      - {name: status, type: enum, enum: OrderStatus}
      - {name: delivery_address, type: text, description: Address as it was at checkout}
      - {name: delivery_instructions, required: false}
      - {name: items_total, type: money}
      - {name: delivery_fee, type: money}
      - {name: discount, type: money, required: false}
      - {name: total, type: money}
      - {name: payment_method, type: enum, required: false, enum: PaymentMethodType}
      - {name: placed_at, type: datetime}
      - {name: eta_minutes, type: int, required: false}
      - {name: courier_name, required: false}
      - {name: courier_phone, required: false}
      - {name: cancel_reason, required: false}
    state_machine:
      field: status
      states: [placed, accepted, preparing, ready, picked_up, delivered, cancelled]
      transitions:
        - {from: placed, target: accepted, 'on': accept}
        - {from: accepted, target: preparing, 'on': prepare}
        - {from: preparing, target: ready, 'on': mark_ready}
        - {from: ready, target: picked_up, 'on': pick_up}
        - {from: picked_up, target: delivered, 'on': deliver}
        - {from: placed, target: cancelled, 'on': cancel}
        - {from: accepted, target: cancelled, 'on': cancel}
    seed_guidance: Three sample orders for the main customer in preparing, picked_up and delivered, so
      tracking can be shown at every step.
  - id: ENT-OrderItem
    name: Order item
    plain_name: Dishes in an order
    fields:
      - {name: order, type: ref, ref: ENT-Order}
      - {name: item, type: ref, ref: ENT-MenuItem}
      - {name: name, description: Dish name at the time of the order}
      - {name: quantity, type: int}
      - {name: selected_options, type: json, required: false}
      - {name: unit_price, type: money}
  - id: ENT-OrderEvent
    name: Order event
    plain_name: Order progress steps
    fields:
      - {name: order, type: ref, ref: ENT-Order}
      - {name: status, type: enum, enum: OrderStatus}
      - {name: note, required: false}
      - {name: at, type: datetime}
  - id: ENT-CourierLocation
    name: Courier location
    plain_name: Courier position
    fields:
      - {name: order, type: ref, ref: ENT-Order}
      - {name: latitude, type: number}
      - {name: longitude, type: number}
      - {name: updated_at, type: datetime}
    seed_guidance: A short route of eight to ten points between the restaurant and the sample address,
      replayed as the courier moves.
  - id: ENT-Courier
    name: Courier
    plain_name: Couriers
    fields:
      - {name: user, type: ref, ref: ENT-User}
      - {name: status, type: enum, enum: CourierStatus}
      - {name: vehicle, required: false}
  - id: ENT-PaymentMethod
    name: Payment method
    plain_name: Saved payment methods
    fields:
      - name: user
        type: ref
        ref: ENT-User
      - name: kind
        type: enum
        enum: PaymentMethodType
      - name: label
        description: Display text only, for example Card ending 4242. Never a full number.
      - name: is_default
        type: bool
  - id: ENT-Payment
    name: Payment
    plain_name: Payments
    fields:
      - {name: order, type: ref, ref: ENT-Order}
      - {name: method, type: enum, enum: PaymentMethodType}
      - {name: status, type: enum, enum: PaymentStatus}
      - {name: amount, type: money}
      - {name: provider_reference, required: false}
  - id: ENT-Rating
    name: Rating
    plain_name: Ratings
    fields:
      - {name: order, type: ref, ref: ENT-Order}
      - {name: restaurant, type: ref, ref: ENT-Restaurant}
      - {name: user, type: ref, ref: ENT-User}
      - {name: food_rating, type: int, description: 1 to 5}
      - {name: delivery_rating, type: int, description: 1 to 5}
      - {name: comment, type: text, required: false}
      - {name: created_at, type: datetime}
    source: research
  - id: ENT-Notification
    name: Notification
    plain_name: Notifications
    fields:
      - {name: user, type: ref, ref: ENT-User}
      - {name: kind, type: enum, enum: NotificationKind}
      - {name: title}
      - {name: body, type: text}
      - {name: is_read, type: bool}
      - {name: created_at, type: datetime}
enums:
  - name: OrderStatus
    values: [placed, accepted, preparing, ready, picked_up, delivered, cancelled]
  - name: PaymentMethodType
    values: [card, wallet, cash_on_delivery]
  - name: PaymentStatus
    values: [pending, paid, failed, refunded]
  - name: OptionKind
    values: [single, multiple]
  - name: NotificationKind
    values: [order_update, offer, account]
  - name: CourierStatus
    values: [offline, available, on_delivery]
seed_guidance: Generate sample records that read like a real business, in the language of the app.
```

## 6. API

```yaml id=API kind=api
operations:
  - id: API-requestOtp
    name: Request sign-in code
    method: POST
    path: /auth/otp
    request_entity: ENT-User
    notes: Sends a one-time code to the phone number. Mock sender in the preview.
  - id: API-verifyOtp
    name: Verify sign-in code
    method: POST
    path: /auth/otp/verify
    request_entity: ENT-User
    response_entity: ENT-User
    notes: Returns the session. New phone numbers create a user.
  - id: API-getMe
    name: Get my profile
    method: GET
    path: /me
    response_entity: ENT-User
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-updateMe
    name: Update my profile
    method: PATCH
    path: /me
    request_entity: ENT-User
    response_entity: ENT-User
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-createAddress
    name: Add an address
    method: POST
    path: /addresses
    request_entity: ENT-Address
    response_entity: ENT-Address
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-listAddresses
    name: List my addresses
    method: GET
    path: /addresses
    response_entity: ENT-Address
    response_many: true
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-updateAddress
    name: Change an address
    method: PUT
    path: /addresses/{id}
    request_entity: ENT-Address
    response_entity: ENT-Address
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-deleteAddress
    name: Delete an address
    method: DELETE
    path: /addresses/{id}
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-listCuisines
    name: List cuisines
    method: GET
    path: /cuisines
    response_entity: ENT-Cuisine
    response_many: true
  - id: API-listRestaurants
    name: List restaurants near me
    method: GET
    path: /restaurants
    response_entity: ENT-Restaurant
    response_many: true
    notes: 'Query: near (latitude and longitude), cuisine, sort, filters, page.'
  - id: API-getRestaurant
    name: Get a restaurant
    method: GET
    path: /restaurants/{id}
    response_entity: ENT-Restaurant
  - id: API-searchRestaurants
    name: Search restaurants and dishes
    method: GET
    path: /search
    response_entity: ENT-Restaurant
    response_many: true
    notes: 'Query: q. Matches restaurant names, cuisines and dish names.'
  - id: API-getMenu
    name: Get a restaurant menu
    method: GET
    path: /restaurants/{id}/menu
    response_entity: ENT-MenuItem
    response_many: true
    notes: Grouped by menu section (ENT-MenuCategory).
  - id: API-getMenuItem
    name: Get a dish with its options
    method: GET
    path: /menu-items/{id}
    response_entity: ENT-MenuItem
    notes: Includes option groups and choices (ENT-OptionGroup, ENT-OptionChoice).
  - id: API-getCart
    name: Get my cart
    method: GET
    path: /cart
    response_entity: ENT-Cart
    auth: authenticated
    notes: Includes its items (ENT-CartItem). One cart, one restaurant.
  - id: API-addCartItem
    name: Add a dish to the cart
    method: POST
    path: /cart/items
    request_entity: ENT-CartItem
    response_entity: ENT-Cart
    auth: authenticated
    notes: Adding from a different restaurant is refused until the cart is cleared.
  - id: API-updateCartItem
    name: Change a cart quantity
    method: PATCH
    path: /cart/items/{id}
    request_entity: ENT-CartItem
    response_entity: ENT-Cart
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-removeCartItem
    name: Remove a dish from the cart
    method: DELETE
    path: /cart/items/{id}
    response_entity: ENT-Cart
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-clearCart
    name: Empty the cart
    method: DELETE
    path: /cart
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-createOrder
    name: Place an order
    method: POST
    path: /orders
    request_entity: ENT-Order
    response_entity: ENT-Order
    auth: authenticated
    notes: Turns the cart into an order and sends it to the restaurant.
  - id: API-listOrders
    name: List my orders
    method: GET
    path: /orders
    response_entity: ENT-Order
    response_many: true
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-getOrder
    name: Get an order
    method: GET
    path: /orders/{id}
    response_entity: ENT-Order
    auth: authenticated
    notes: Includes its dishes (ENT-OrderItem).
  - id: API-cancelOrder
    name: Cancel an order
    method: POST
    path: /orders/{id}/cancel
    response_entity: ENT-Order
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-getOrderTracking
    name: Get order progress
    method: GET
    path: /orders/{id}/tracking
    response_entity: ENT-OrderEvent
    response_many: true
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-getCourierLocation
    name: Get the courier position
    method: GET
    path: /orders/{id}/courier-location
    response_entity: ENT-CourierLocation
    auth: authenticated
    notes: Polled every few seconds while the order is on its way. Mock route in the preview.
  - id: API-listPaymentMethods
    name: List saved payment methods
    method: GET
    path: /payment-methods
    response_entity: ENT-PaymentMethod
    response_many: true
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-addPaymentMethod
    name: Save a payment method
    method: POST
    path: /payment-methods
    request_entity: ENT-PaymentMethod
    response_entity: ENT-PaymentMethod
    auth: authenticated
    notes: The provider tokenizes the card; only the display label is stored.
  - id: API-removePaymentMethod
    name: Remove a payment method
    method: DELETE
    path: /payment-methods/{id}
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-createPayment
    name: Pay for an order
    method: POST
    path: /payments
    request_entity: ENT-Payment
    response_entity: ENT-Payment
    auth: authenticated
    notes: Mock provider by default.
  - id: API-createRating
    name: Rate an order
    method: POST
    path: /orders/{id}/rating
    request_entity: ENT-Rating
    response_entity: ENT-Rating
    auth: authenticated
    source: research
  - id: API-listRestaurantRatings
    name: List restaurant ratings
    method: GET
    path: /restaurants/{id}/ratings
    response_entity: ENT-Rating
    response_many: true
    source: research
  - id: API-listNotifications
    name: List my notifications
    method: GET
    path: /notifications
    response_entity: ENT-Notification
    response_many: true
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-markNotificationRead
    name: Mark a notification read
    method: POST
    path: /notifications/{id}/read
    response_entity: ENT-Notification
    auth: authenticated
  - id: API-registerPushToken
    name: Register this phone for push
    method: POST
    path: /devices/push-token
    auth: authenticated
    notes: Body carries the device token. Mock in the preview.
mock_guidance: A generated mock backend answers every operation; nothing leaves the device in the preview.
```

## 7. Roles

```yaml id=ROLES kind=roles
roles:
  - {id: ROLE-customer, name: Customer, description: Orders food and follows the delivery.}
```

## 8. Integrations

```yaml id=INTEGRATIONS kind=integrations
items:
  - id: INT-sms_otp
    name: Sign-in codes by SMS
    purpose: Send one-time codes so people can sign in with a phone number.
    notes: Mock sender prints the code in the preview. A real SMS provider is chosen at release.
  - id: INT-maps
    name: Maps and geocoding
    purpose: Show restaurants and the courier on a map and turn a map pin into an address.
    notes: Static sample map in the preview. A real map provider key is needed at release.
  - id: INT-payments
    name: Payments
    purpose: Take card and wallet payments through a payment provider.
    notes: Mock provider by default. A real provider SDK needs a development build and keeps card data
      off our servers. Online payment only.
  - id: INT-push_notifications
    name: Push notifications
    purpose: Send order status and offers to the phone.
    notes: Shown as in-app banners in the preview.
  - id: INT-plan_for_a_development_build
    name: Plan for a development build
    purpose: Services with native code need an Expo development build instead of the stock preview client.
    source: research
    research_ref: RA-003
  - id: INT-send_codes_and_reminders_from_the_server
    name: Send codes and reminders from the server
    purpose: Text messages and reminders are sent through a provider API from a server, not from the app.
    source: research
    research_ref: RA-004
```

## 9. Behavior

```yaml id=BEHAVIOR kind=behavior
offline: Basic cache. The last loaded lists and details stay readable without a connection, and changes
  wait on the phone until the connection returns.
deep_links:
  - /menu-item/[id]
  - /orders/[id]
  - /orders/[id]/rate
  - /orders/[id]/tracking
  - /restaurant/[id]
  - /restaurant/[id]/ratings
notifications: [order update notifications, offer notifications, account notifications]
permission_prompts:
  - Location, only while the app is open and only when the person uses a nearby or map feature
  - Notifications, asked after the first useful moment and not at launch
error_conventions:
  - Show a plain-language message and a retry action, never a raw error code
  - Keep what the person typed when a request fails
  - Loading, empty, error and offline states come from the screen recipe
  - 'Never log personal data (data classification: internal)'
accessibility:
  - Every control has a text label for screen readers
  - Text meets WCAG AA contrast in light and dark mode
  - Text grows with the phone's font size setting
  - Touch targets are at least 44 by 44 points
```

## 10. Screens

### SCR-001 - /welcome

```yaml id=SCR-001 kind=screen
route: /welcome
recipe: welcome
purpose: Introduce the app to a signed-out visitor and offer to sign in, create an account or look around
flow: FLW-002
sections: [help_hint]
actions:
  - sign_in: {go: SCR-002}
  - create_account: {go: SCR-003}
  - browse_as_guest: {go: SCR-004}
copy:
  cta_guest: Browse restaurants
  cta_primary: Sign in
  cta_secondary: Create account
  intro: Introduce the app to a signed-out visitor and offer to sign in, create an account or look around
  title: Hungry? We deliver
checks:
  - Browse restaurants opens the home screen without asking for an account
  - Sign in and Create account open the matching screens
  - 'Everything this screen promises works: introduce the app to a signed-out visitor and offer to sign
    in, create an account or look around'
```

### SCR-002 - /login

```yaml id=SCR-002 kind=screen
route: /login
recipe: login-otp
purpose: Sign in with a phone number and a one-time code
flow: FLW-002
sections: [help_hint]
actions:
  - send_code: {calls: API-requestOtp, on_success: show the code field and start the resend timer}
  - verify_code: {calls: API-verifyOtp, go: SCR-004, on_success: save the session and open the home screen}
  - new_user_setup: {go: SCR-003, on_success: opened instead of home when the number is new}
states:
  wrong_code: {allow: 'retry, and resend after 30 seconds', show: inline error under the code field}
copy:
  cta: Send code
  hint: We will text you a 6-digit code
  intro: Sign in with a phone number and a one-time code
  title: Sign in
checks:
  - A wrong code shows an error and allows another try
  - The resend link stays disabled for 30 seconds after a send
  - 'Everything this screen promises works: sign in with a phone number and a one-time code'
```

